WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:04.310
- [Mark] Yeah, so
Patricia, what's going on?

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:05.930
- I'm dying.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.950
And I'm a fellow HIV,

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:09.950
cancer,

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.310
my chest.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.920
- [Mark] So you went to the doctor when?

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.661
- Two weeks ago when I had two strokes.

00:00:15.661 --> 00:00:16.776
- [Mark] You had a stroke?

00:00:16.776 --> 00:00:17.680
- Two strokes.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:18.620
- [Mark] Two strokes?

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.461
- Yeah.

00:00:19.461 --> 00:00:20.365
- [Mark] And you went to the doctor?

00:00:20.365 --> 00:00:22.770
- Yeah, I found out I was sick.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.025
- [Mark] When you found
you have lung cancer?

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.443
- Breast cancer.

00:00:27.498 --> 00:00:30.920
- [Mark] And you're HIV positive?

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:31.753
- Yeah.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.913
- [Mark] Wow. How do you
think you picked up HIV?

00:00:38.189 --> 00:00:40.713
- By someone doing
something fucked up to me.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.773
- [Mark] You had sex with somebody...

00:00:43.773 --> 00:00:45.340
- When I was asleep, they had sex with me.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.137
- [Mark] Oh, that happens here.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.893
- So, I'm telling my story now.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.843
It's my last time telling my story.

00:00:55.744 --> 00:00:56.911
So, that's me.

00:00:58.697 --> 00:01:00.490
- [Mark] So what are you gonna do now?

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.492
What do the doctors say
about your lung cancer?

00:01:03.492 --> 00:01:04.767
- It'll kill me off-

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:05.991
- [Mark] Breast cancer.

00:01:05.991 --> 00:01:06.824
- It'll kill me off because

00:01:06.824 --> 00:01:09.263
it spread through my body already.

00:01:10.693 --> 00:01:11.993
- [Mark] It spread through your body?

00:01:11.993 --> 00:01:12.826
- Already.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.463
So I get real sleepy and shit.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:21.323
So I'ma sleep my time away
until it's time for me to go.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:25.630
It's getting cold out here too.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.970
- [Mark] Yeah, it's getting cold.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.920
- So I don't know if I'm gonna make it.

00:01:30.946 --> 00:01:31.919
- [Mark] How old are you now?

00:01:31.919 --> 00:01:33.833
- 33, I'll be 34 December 1st.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:43.670
- [Mark] How are you processing
all this new information?

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.518
Are you back to using again?

00:01:45.518 --> 00:01:48.477
- No, I don't use anymore.

00:01:48.477 --> 00:01:49.930
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.690
Sometimes stress brings...

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.863
- Yeah, sometimes it's that way.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:59.468
- [Mark] Do you have any
family you can go see?

00:01:59.468 --> 00:02:00.301
- No.

00:02:00.301 --> 00:02:01.634
- [Mark] Nobody.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.863
You're just living on
your own and that's that?

00:02:07.466 --> 00:02:10.720
(cars pass by)

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.020
- Tell everybody my story.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.684
That's it.
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:02:20.684 --> 00:02:22.213
- That's it.

00:02:23.217 --> 00:02:24.532
(car zooms by)

00:02:24.532 --> 00:02:26.115
- [Mark] All right.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.247
All I can say is good
luck to you. I hope...

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:39.240
- I hope I'd be in a
better place...up there.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.073
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:40.073 --> 00:02:41.809
This is about as bad as
place as you can ever find.

00:02:41.809 --> 00:02:42.642
- Yeah.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.273
Thank you.

00:02:57.093 --> 00:02:57.926
Good Morning.

00:02:57.926 --> 00:02:59.360
- [Mark] All right, Patricia.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.193
How are you?

00:03:00.193 --> 00:03:01.140
- Okay.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.878
- [Mark] So what's the latest?

00:03:02.878 --> 00:03:03.957
- January 18.

00:03:03.957 --> 00:03:06.086
- [Mark] January 18th
you're gonna start with-

00:03:06.086 --> 00:03:06.919
- Chemotherapy.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:09.260
- [Mark] Chemotherapy. Good for you.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.093
Good for you.

00:03:10.093 --> 00:03:11.339
Because you were debating
whether to do that or not, right?

00:03:11.339 --> 00:03:12.172
- Yep.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:13.957
I'ma do it.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.857
- [Mark] So when you wake up
in the morning, do you go,

00:03:16.857 --> 00:03:18.510
